README

These are the Fandol fonts for Chinese typesetting.
Current version of Fandol fonts contains four
styles: Song, Hei, Kai, Fang.
All the fonts are OpenType.

These fonts are developed by Fandol team.
The member of Fandol team: Clerk Ma & Jie Su.

These fonts's licensing is GPL + GPL font exception.

CHANGELOG

v0.1 2013/07/31
    * initital version.
v0.2 2013/08/03
    * change GID to CID (Adobe-GB1-5)
    * using AFDKO to compile to OpenType
    * CID ranges: 940-7702, 7717-8895, 29064-30220
    * XUID: 1440
    * fontforge + inkscape as outline editor
v0.3 2015/07/18
    * added two braille fonts
    * fixed bugs of kanji fonts
v0.4 2026/11/21
    * updated braille fonts (rebuild name table, and moved to fandol-braille package)
    * marked kanji fonts obsolete (and moved to CTAN's obsolete directory)

ADDENDUM

自思源黑体和思源宋体发布十多年来，
本项目中所涉及的宋和黑两个风格的字体已经完成了其历史使命。
随着各种字体厂商的增多，楷和仿宋两种风格，
也几乎唾手可得，授权价格极为低廉。
故此，本项目字体，盲文移至fandol-braille。
汉字字体贸然删除可能会影响到一些包，
故CTAN上依旧会保留一份副本，标为废弃，以供备考。

Since the release of Source Han Sans and Source Han Serif more than a decade ago,
the Song and Hei style fonts involved in this project have fulfilled their historical mission.
With the proliferation of various font vendors, the Kai and Fang styles are also nearly readily available,
and their licensing costs are extremely low.
Therefore, the Braille fonts of this project are moved to fandol-braille.
Rashly deleting the Chinese character fonts may affect some packages,
so a copy will still be retained on CTAN, marked as obsolete, for reference.
